# CI gate — do not finish until green

Before you report work as **done**, **complete**, or **ready to push**, run the same checks as `.github/workflows/ci.yml`:

```bash
# Preferred (any OS) — single task list
python scripts/ci.py

# Wrappers (same entrypoint):
.\scripts\ci.ps1          # Windows
./scripts/ci.sh           # Linux / Pi / macOS
```

`scripts/ci.py` is the SSOT: install (unless `--skip-install`), Ruff check + format check, ShellCheck, LF/CSS/fixture/shell checks, Pyright, vulture, pytest. Pytest flags (`-m not live`, coverage) come from `pyproject.toml` — do not restate them in CI scripts.

CI uses **check-only** Ruff (`ruff check`, `ruff format --check`) so a push cannot pass locally while GitHub fails because pre-commit auto-fixed files in the runner. Run `ruff check --fix && ruff format` before commit, or use pre-commit hooks locally (`pre-commit install`). Locally, `python scripts/ci.py --fix` applies Ruff fixes then re-runs checks.

## Required workflow

1. After substantive edits (source, tests, scripts, workflow, pre-commit config), run the CI script.
2. If anything fails, fix it and re-run until all steps pass.
3. Only then commit, push, or tell the user the task is finished.

Do not skip this because tests alone passed — **pre-commit** (ruff, shellcheck, LF) and **pyright** must pass too. That is what failed in CI previously.

## When it applies

- New features, bug fixes, refactors, test changes, dependency or workflow edits.
- Skip only for pure docs with zero code/tooling changes, or when the user explicitly asks not to run checks.
